From 6e41c12f290ef17789bf207159c989563c0b98c1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 16:28:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] feat(intake): add public intake API contract and
 client-side validation

First slice of A1 (public questionnaire). No UI yet - this is the
contract and the validation layer the wizard will sit on.

validation.ts mirrors the backend domain rules 1:1 so the form cannot
accept a value the server will reject:
- CzechBirthNumber: Normalize (optional slash after 6th digit),
  DecodeMonth (+50 female, +20/+70 alternates), century split at 53,
  forbidden '000' serial on 9-digit, modulo-11 on 10-digit
- InsuranceNumber CZ policy (^d{9,10}$, structure only)
- CzechHealthInsurerCode 111/201/205/207/209/211/213
- Email: exactly one '@', local <= 64, total <= 254
- Phone: structural E.164 gate; libphonenumber stays server-side
  rather than shipping ~150kB to a public bundle for one field

Adds a cross-check the spec does not ask for: when both a birth number
and a date of birth/sex are supplied they must agree. A mistyped birth
number is the most common way bad identity data reaches the matching
pipeline, and it is cheapest to catch at the field.

publicIntake.ts uses its own axios instance, NOT the shared client:
that one attaches a bearer token and redirects to /login on 401, which
would bounce an anonymous patient out of a half-filled questionnaire.

Idempotency-Key is one uuid per questionnaire session held in
sessionStorage, so a double-tapped Submit cannot create two patients.
All storage access is try/catch guarded for private-mode browsers.

Typecheck: 0 errors in new files; repo total unchanged at 581.

